[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"390","stub":{"id":"390","section":"02. Redcliff to Tigiwon Rd/FR 707","altname":"Gilman Gorge","river":"Eagle River","difficulty":"IVtoVstandoutVplus","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"92","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"1372","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Put-in","distance":"0","photoID":"8062","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The first 2 miles consists of fast-moving, read and run class III and IV rapids.","id":"1373","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Upper Half","distance":"0","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"You can't miss it.","id":"1374","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Gilman Mine","distance":"2","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false,"photoID":"884424"},{"type":"waterfall","description":"Starts at railroad overpass. Fall Creek comes in on the left. Longest rapid of the run. Builds up to 10' crux drop about 2/3 of the way down, which becomes a sticky hole at higher flows. Technical run-out. Scout before the bridge or just after.","id":"1375","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Fall Creek Rapid","distance":"2.2","difficulty":"V","approximate":false,"photoID":"8060"},{"type":"waterfall","description":"Can be run down right or left channel.","id":"1376","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"S-turn Rapid","distance":"2.5","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"waterfall","description":"Fun, technical 5' boof in the middle of this one.","id":"1377","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Boof Rapid","distance":"2.6","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false,"photoID":"8057"},{"type":"portage","description":"This double drop rapid is identified by a large rock tower on river right. Look for a riverwide log at the entrance, which may need portaging, depending on water level. UPDATE - in the Spring of '04 local boates cut out the left end of the log, creating a means for passage without a portage.","id":"1378","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Tower Rapid","distance":"2.8","photoID":"8059","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Primarily read and run with a few holes to punch.","id":"1379","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Boogie Water","distance":"3","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"1/2 mile of class II.","id":"1380","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Slackwater","distance":"3.1","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"hazard","description":"Contrary to CRC, most local boaters run this rapid on a regular basis. A definite scout for a newbie. This steep and manky rapid starts at the railroad bridge and contains some artificial hazards. Watch out for the sticky \"guardian hole\" located directly under the bridge, which is generally snuck on the right or left. Lots of sharp rocks so stay upright. Although AW rates this as a \"Standard Rated Rapid\" of 5.2 difficulty, this rapid is probably better classified as a 5.1 at low to medium flows and a 5.2 at high water.","id":"1381","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Slurry Pipe Rapid","distance":"3.6","photoID":"8061","difficulty":"V+","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Tigawon Road (FR 707).","id":"1382","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Take-out","distance":"4","photoID":null,"difficulty":null,"approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"D6HRUXCimARQh88mMwRjq","title":"Wood free as of summer 2020","post_date":"2021-03-29 06:21:45+00","detail":null,"user":{"name":"Erik Larsson"}},{"id":"101249328","title":null,"post_date":"2012-06-02 04:00:00+00","detail":"Large River Wide telephone pole is currently at the top of Fall Creek Rapid. You can get out at the bridge and put in where the pole is wedged in. Will update this summer when we can get it out.\n\nAs of Late May 2012 the log was pulled up on shore. It will be back in the river with high water of 2013 if its still there next season.","user":{"name":"Craig Phillips"}}],"photos":[{"id":"884423","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"The Mine on Gilman Gorge near the start of the run.","caption":"Mine","poi_name":"","subject":"Eric Bessette and Mike Rausch","author":"Thomas O'Keefe ©","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:48:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884423","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884423"}},{"id":"8062","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"","caption":"Gilman Gorge - Put-in","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe ©","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:48:37.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8062","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8062"}},{"id":"884424","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"The Mine on Gilman Gorge near the start of the run.","caption":"Mine","poi_name":"","subject":"Mike Rausch","author":"Thomas O'Keefe ©","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:49:04.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884424","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884424"}},{"id":"884422","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"Looking down from the start of Slurry Pipe rapid.","caption":"Slurry Pipe","poi_name":"Slurry Pipe","subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe ©","poi_id":"1378","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:49:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884422","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884422"}},{"id":"8061","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"","caption":"Gilman Gorge - Slurry Pipe - Bottom Half","poi_name":"Slurry Pipe Rapid","subject":"Eric Bessette","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"1378","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:50:08.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8061","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8061"}},{"id":"8060","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"","caption":"Gilman Gorge - Fall Creek First Drop","poi_name":"Fall Creek - First Drop","subject":"Eric Bessette","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"1375","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:49:31.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8060","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8060"}},{"id":"8058","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"","caption":"Gilman Gorge - Fall Creek Crux","poi_name":"Fall Creek Crux","subject":"Eric Bessette","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"1375","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:49:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8058","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8058"}},{"id":"8059","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"","caption":"Gilman Gorge - Tower Rapid","poi_name":"Tower Rapid","subject":"Eric Bessette","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"1378","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:50:19.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8059","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8059"}},{"id":"8057","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1716","description":"","caption":"Gilman Gorge - Boof Rapid","poi_name":"Boof Rapid","subject":"Mike Rausch","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"1378","photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2024-09-27T16:50:31.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8057","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8057"}}],"detail":{"id":"390","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Gilman Gorge is a classic run in the high country characterized by consistent class 4/5 rapids for four miles. It can be run from ~200 to 1500 CFS (the run changes character above 700). The top half is classic class 4/5 boogie water followed by two miles of class 5 drops. One you pass Fall Creek on the left be ready for the run to change character.\n\nThe run used to have a reputation of being manky, with mining and railroad debris, but this was cleaned up recently and is now mostly clean (with the exception of Slurry Pipe Rapid).\n\nScouting and portaging are easy to do throughout the gorge.\n\n**Logistics:** This is a convenient creek run close to Vail and a popular evening run with the locals. Take exit 171 off I-70 just west of Vail onto Hwy. 24. Head 4.7 miles south on Hwy. 24 and just before crossing the Eagle River turn right onto Tigwon Road. Follow this road 0.5 miles to a pull-out along the Eagle River that serves as a take-out. To reach the put-in return to Hwy. 24 and head south up river. After a few miles of climbing up the hill you will cross a high arch bridge. After crossing this bridge take the dirt road that leads down to the river to a small parking area at the confluence of Homestake Creek and the Eagle River. Alternatively continue up Hwy 24 which now parallels [Homestake Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3415/) and add the steep drops of this classic creek as an jump start to Gilman. Note that CRC mentions parking on the highway, but in the past few years, parking at the river level hasn't been a problem. There no longer seems to be any issues at the put-in or take-out, in regards to private property and the authorities.","averageGradient":"120","maxGradient":"140","length":"4.4","correlations":[{"reachID":"390","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComm